ther eye or pull the whole beret evenly across both eyebrows. If <image3> instead shows a structured cap or another non-beret hat, preserve that hat type and brim shape; wear its brim close above BOTH eyebrows without touching or hiding either eyebrow. If <image3> has no hat, do not add one. Arrange the original hair tucked beneath the chosen headwear, with no fringe lifting the band away from the brow. Straight front view facing the camera. The scarf knot and hanging tails stay on the chest, with front patches only on the front. If footwear is unseen use simple matching shoes. Preserve natural facial detail. Avoid: multiple people, duplicate person, collage, text, watermark, cropped feet, cropped head, extra limbs, deformed hands, different clothes, different identity, fisheye.",
